{"code":200,"message":"OK","tweet":{"url":"https://x.com/Bober_smart/status/2103581364134256863","id":"2103581364134256863","text":"https://x.com/i/article/2103570915359346688","raw_text":{"text":"https://t.co/7vLHBOOfNw","display_text_range":[0,23],"facets":[{"type":"url","indices":[0,23],"original":"https://t.co/7vLHBOOfNw","replacement":"https://x.com/i/article/2103570915359346688","display":"x.com/i/article/2103…"}]},"author":{"screen_name":"Bober_smart","url":"https://x.com/Bober_smart","id":"1986121366232559616","followers":14994,"following":804,"likes":113993,"media_count":1085,"name":"Bober_smart","description":"AI Builder | Technologies | Testing","raw_description":{"text":"AI Builder | Technologies | Testing","facets":[]},"location":"San Francisco","banner_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/1986121366232559616/1777675826","avatar_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2050347090543300608/p1PlS_hc_200x200.jpg","joined":"Wed Nov 05 17:20:20 +0000 2025","protected":false,"website":null,"verification":{"verified":true,"verified_at":null,"type":"individual"},"avatar_color":null},"replies":20,"retweets":5,"likes":80,"bookmarks":102,"quotes":16,"created_at":"Fri Sep 25 20:24:14 +0000 2026","created_timestamp":1790367854,"possibly_sensitive":false,"views":114482,"is_note_tweet":false,"community_note":null,"lang":null,"replying_to":null,"replying_to_status":null,"article":{"created_at":"2026-09-25T20:24:14.000Z","modified_at":"2026-09-25T20:24:14.000Z","id":"2103570915359346688","title":"Full guide to Jev 10 steps for setup","preview_text":"You will learn, in 10 steps, how to strip expensive LLM calls out of your agent and replace them with a separate decision-making layer.\nEvery agent has the same leak: an expensive language model sits","cover_media":{"id":"QXBpTWVkaWE6DAAFCgABHTFrwpQW0AAKAAIbkB7cExrwAAAA","media_id":"2103580984411082752","media_info":{"__typename":"ApiImage","color_info":{"palette":[{"percentage":51.07,"rgb":{"blue":144,"green":107,"red":227}},{"percentage":18.28,"rgb":{"blue":26,"green":24,"red":37}},{"percentage":16.74,"rgb":{"blue":191,"green":191,"red":205}},{"percentage":12.44,"rgb":{"blue":95,"green":74,"red":138}},{"percentage":0.87,"rgb":{"blue":60,"green":40,"red":83}}]},"original_img_height":512,"original_img_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTFrwpQW0AAH0qx.jpg","original_img_width":1280},"media_key":"3_2103580984411082752"},"content":{"blocks":[{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[{"length":135,"offset":0,"style":"Bold"}],"key":"dddq2","text":"You will learn, in 10 steps, how to strip expensive LLM calls out of your agent and replace them with a separate decision-making layer.","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"b0v2e","text":"Every agent has the same leak: an expensive language model sits in a loop answering yes-or-no, picking the next worker, and scoring a source. Those calls never needed generation. They need a model built to decide.  ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{"urls":[{"fromIndex":288,"text":"docs.typesafe.ai","toIndex":304}]},"entityRanges":[{"key":0,"length":16,"offset":288}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"23qii","text":"Jev is TypeSafe AI’s System One model. You give it state and options. It returns a typed answer and a confidence score. It will not write your briefing, generate code, or explain itself in prose. It decides, fast and cheap: about $0.042 per million input tokens, with output tokens free. docs.typesafe.ai ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[{"length":69,"offset":0,"style":"Bold"}],"key":"1qia9","text":"An LLM does the work → Jev chooses what happens next → code executes.","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[{"key":1,"length":1,"offset":0}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"ao1vk","text":" ","type":"atomic"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[{"length":53,"offset":0,"style":"Bold"}],"key":"eql6b","text":"Step 01. Find the part of the agent Jev can take over ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[{"length":7,"offset":67,"style":"Italic"},{"length":5,"offset":110,"style":"Italic"},{"length":6,"offset":129,"style":"Italic"},{"length":9,"offset":158,"style":"Italic"}],"key":"fpglc","text":"Before any code, split the agent’s calls into two piles. If a step creates text, it stays with the LLM. If it picks from a list, scores something, or answers yes or no, it belongs to Jev.  ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"8mb3h","text":"Fetching sources, writing paragraphs, and saving files stay with tools and generative models. “Who acts next?” and “Is this source relevant?” are Jev work. A hard rule such as “stop after ten actions” is code, not a model.  ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"4jnv2","text":"The test is simple: if it produces text, keep the LLM. If it picks, scores, or answers yes/no, use Jev.","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[{"key":2,"length":1,"offset":0}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"4up98","text":" ","type":"atomic"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[{"length":44,"offset":0,"style":"Bold"}],"key":"3sm64","text":"Step 02. Design the state Jev actually reads ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{"urls":[{"fromIndex":159,"text":"docs.typesafe.ai","toIndex":175}]},"entityRanges":[{"key":3,"length":16,"offset":159}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"2p5q2","text":"Jev does not go looking for context. It judges only what you put in state. Vague input produces a vague decision. That is how official state docs describe it. docs.typesafe.ai   ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"fh346","text":"Give it evidence, not vibes: the goal, the sources, what has already been found, and what is still missing. Then the answer can be sharp instead of “probably that way”","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[{"length":59,"offset":0,"style":"Bold"}],"key":"2lhmg","text":"Step 03. Test one question in the official Playground first ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{"urls":[{"fromIndex":84,"text":"console.typesafe.ai","toIndex":103}]},"entityRanges":[{"key":4,"length":19,"offset":84}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"4h5fm","text":"Do not wire the API until you have seen one live answer. Open the TypeSafe console: console.typesafe.ai. Paste the state. Ask a single question: “Which worker should act next?”  ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"d4tto","text":"Keep the options as a closed list. Watch the typed answer and the confidence score. If the choice is wrong, the fix is almost always the evidence in the state, not “a different model”","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[{"key":5,"length":1,"offset":0}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"9s114","text":" ","type":"atomic"},{"data":{"urls":[{"fromIndex":12,"text":"docs.typesafe.ai/introduction/quickstart","toIndex":52},{"fromIndex":54,"text":"docs.typesafe.ai","toIndex":70}]},"entityRanges":[{"key":6,"length":40,"offset":12},{"key":7,"length":16,"offset":54}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"9bbmb","text":"Quickstart: docs.typesafe.ai/introduction/quickstart. docs.typesafe.ai","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[{"length":39,"offset":0,"style":"Bold"}],"key":"d7ikf","text":"Step 04. Learn the three question types ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"6q6pj","text":"TypeSafe’s official primitives:  ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[{"length":6,"offset":0,"style":"Bold"}],"key":"26j28","text":"Choice — routing: pick one option from a list","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[{"length":5,"offset":0,"style":"Bold"}],"key":"621da","text":"Score — a value on a rubric you define","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[{"length":4,"offset":0,"style":"Bold"}],"key":"8bl52","text":"Noul — probability of “yes,” from 0 to 1  ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{"urls":[{"fromIndex":119,"text":"docs.typesafe.ai","toIndex":135}]},"entityRanges":[{"key":8,"length":16,"offset":119}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"2947f","text":"Choice routes. Score ranks. Noul gates. Yes/no, pick-one, and rank-this no longer have to go through a frontier model. docs.typesafe.ai","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[{"length":41,"offset":0,"style":"Bold"}],"key":"7apck","text":"Step 05. Narrow a long list with a funnel ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"6ieiu","text":"Choice can hold up to 255 options, but the cleaner pattern is a chain: code drops the obvious misses → Score ranks what is left → Choice makes the final pick.  ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"i1bh","text":"That is how you select one candidate from dozens. Each layer is cheap, and the final call is easier to defend.","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[{"length":58,"offset":0,"style":"Bold"}],"key":"bc2iq","text":"Step 06. Put a dispatcher between shared state and workers ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"29vo3","text":"Jev’s place in an agent team is not “another chat in the middle.” It sits between shared state and the workers.  ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"bm312","text":"State holds the goal, progress, and evidence. Jev decides. A dispatcher hands the job off. Research, writing, and human review write results back into the same state. The loop closes. Jev generates nothing. It only says who acts, and when.","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[{"key":9,"length":1,"offset":0}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"d0smu","text":" ","type":"atomic"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"cdd8v","text":"The same idea shows up in a browser agent: the page exposes a fresh action menu, Jev picks the next click. Browser Use × TypeSafe demo: Zurich → London in about seven seconds.","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[{"key":10,"length":1,"offset":0}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"5u6jt","text":" ","type":"atomic"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[{"length":56,"offset":0,"style":"Bold"}],"key":"a5mde","text":"Step 07. Stop paying for questions to wait on each other ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{"urls":[{"fromIndex":283,"text":"docs.typesafe.ai","toIndex":299}]},"entityRanges":[{"key":11,"length":16,"offset":283}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"ddv7s","text":"A dispatcher often needs a worker, an urgency score, and an approval check at once. If all three can read the same state, send them in one request. Questions run in parallel and cannot see one another’s answers. If a decision needs a fresh search, run the search first, then decide. docs.typesafe.ai","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[{"length":52,"offset":0,"style":"Bold"}],"key":"b3v1e","text":"Step 08. Add the harness: model router and tool gate ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"felqb","text":"Two Jev layers. Neither writes text.  ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"4qt7t","text":"On top: which model this request actually needs — cheap or strong.  ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"bj8iu","text":"At the bottom: whether a dangerous tool call is blocked before it runs.  ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"assof","text":"A frontier model should no longer be called just to ask “is this request simple?” or “is this command safe?” Those are decisions. Decisions go to Jev.","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[{"length":53,"offset":0,"style":"Bold"}],"key":"eam4g","text":"Step 09. Compact context with a filter, not a rewrite ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"e38pe","text":"Classic compaction is a “summarize the history” prompt. That is generation again: slow and lossy.  ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"3qvld","text":"Jev scores each entry and drops the rest. That is not a summary. It is a relevance filter. The original write-up cites Alex Volkov’s measurement: about one second, a Claude session from nearly a million tokens down to ~86K.  ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"6necg","text":"A summarizer rewrites. A filter keeps or deletes. The second job is a decision.","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[{"length":53,"offset":0,"style":"Bold"}],"key":"6t6fh","text":"Step 10. Count the generation you just stopped buying ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{"urls":[{"fromIndex":340,"text":"typesafe.ai","toIndex":351}]},"entityRanges":[{"key":12,"length":11,"offset":340}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"9g50c","text":"$0.042 per million input tokens, output free. At 1,000 input tokens per decision, ten thousand forks cost about 42 cents of Jev inference. The same ten thousand yes/no calls through a frontier model are a different order of magnitude. The agent did not get smarter. You stopped paying a generation price for work that was never generation. typesafe.ai   ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"d6qfs","text":"TypeSafe’s official chart: intelligence on System One tasks versus workflow cost.","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[{"key":13,"length":1,"offset":0}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"5a5vs","text":" ","type":"atomic"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[{"length":9,"offset":0,"style":"Bold"}],"key":"5k7io","text":"The shift ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"ahid8","text":"Let the LLM research, write, and generate.  ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"5tdqq","text":"Let Jev route, score, approve, or escalate.  ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"42r","text":"Let code execute the decision.  ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"2dgct","text":"Jev is not another chatbot. It is a fast decision layer that reads the current state of your system and chooses among the options you define. The real edge is not the seven-second flight demo. It is how many expensive calls inside your agents never needed to emit a single token of text.  ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"ki4l","text":"Install the decision layer once. Measure it. Then replace the next expensive fork.","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"c9m0","text":"","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"9va2r","text":"Thanks for watching","type":"header-one"}],"entityMap":[{"key":"12","value":{"data":{"url":"https://typesafe.ai/blog/introducing-system-one-models-and-jev"},"mutability":"Mutable","type":"LINK"}},{"key":"8","value":{"data":{"url":"https://docs.typesafe.ai/introduction"},"mutability":"Mutable","type":"LINK"}},{"key":"4","value":{"data":{"url":"https://console.typesafe.ai/"},"mutability":"Mutable","type":"LINK"}},{"key":"11","value":{"data":{"url":"https://docs.typesafe.ai/introduction"},"mutability":"Mutable","type":"LINK"}},{"key":"9","value":{"data":{"entityKey":"3223f9b0-e894-44b8-b0f5-ff9b883ef4d9","mediaItems":[{"localMediaId":"37","mediaCategory":"DraftTweetImage","mediaId":"2103579038576971776"}]},"mutability":"Immutable","type":"MEDIA"}},{"key":"13","value":{"data":{"entityKey":"4cfee5bc-b0bc-44aa-9300-cc0de1fb0afa","mediaItems":[{"localMediaId":"43","mediaCategory":"DraftTweetImage","mediaId":"2103580095487053824"}]},"mutability":"Immutable","type":"MEDIA"}},{"key":"5","value":{"data":{"entityKey":"091da8e9-9df5-4e58-8531-c61652f4f3a1","mediaItems":[{"localMediaId":"35","mediaCategory":"DraftTweetImage","mediaId":"2103578367408713728"}]},"mutability":"Immutable","type":"MEDIA"}},{"key":"10","value":{"data":{"entityKey":"1bcebdfe-c1b0-4a26-ade4-7d0f73516ae7","mediaItems":[{"localMediaId":"39","mediaCategory":"DraftTweetImage","mediaId":"2103579209650106368"}]},"mutability":"Immutable","type":"MEDIA"}},{"key":"6","value":{"data":{"url":"https://docs.typesafe.ai/introduction/quickstart"},"mutability":"Mutable","type":"LINK"}},{"key":"1","value":{"data":{"entityKey":"912a7a52-6591-40a6-8de7-5765723fd134","mediaItems":[{"localMediaId":"31","mediaCategory":"DraftTweetImage","mediaId":"2103576846654713856"}]},"mutability":"Immutable","type":"MEDIA"}},{"key":"0","value":{"data":{"url":"https://docs.typesafe.ai/models"},"mutability":"Mutable","type":"LINK"}},{"key":"2","value":{"data":{"entityKey":"57666ec4-fde5-457a-8c09-aaec52b6318a","mediaItems":[{"localMediaId":"33","mediaCategory":"DraftTweetImage","mediaId":"2103577900758831104"}]},"mutability":"Immutable","type":"MEDIA"}},{"key":"7","value":{"data":{"url":"https://docs.typesafe.ai/introduction/quickstart"},"mutability":"Mutable","type":"LINK"}},{"key":"3","value":{"data":{"url":"https://docs.typesafe.ai/concepts/state"},"mutability":"Mutable","type":"LINK"}}]},"media_entities":[{"id":"QXBpTWVkaWE6DAAFCgABHTFpYUKXsAAKAAIbkB7cExrwAAAA","media_id":"2103578367408713728","media_info":{"__typename":"ApiImage","color_info":{"palette":[{"percentage":60.87,"rgb":{"blue":31,"green":31,"red":31}},{"percentage":24.87,"rgb":{"blue":246,"green":239,"red":234}},{"percentage":13.44,"rgb":{"blue":114,"green":116,"red":116}},{"percentage":1,"rgb":{"blue":235,"green":98,"red":36}},{"percentage":0.46,"rgb":{"blue":15,"green":15,"red":88}}]},"original_img_height":802,"original_img_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/med